.TH WMAPPS 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmapps \- list, launch and generate menus from installed desktop applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmapps
list | json | skipped | icons [\-\-size \fIN\fR] | menu [\-t \fIterm\fR] [\-o \fIfile\fR] | launch \fIID\fR [\fIFILE\fR|\fIURL\fR...] | exec \fIID\fR [\fIFILE\fR|\fIURL\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads XDG .desktop files (system, user and Flatpak exports), applies OnlyShowIn/NotShowIn for Window Maker, expands the
Exec field codes, and prints the result as a list, JSON, an icon list (PNG/XPM, converted from SVG when a converter is
installed, otherwise generated) or a Window Maker menu.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-dir " D"
Extra applications directory (also used by the tests).
.TP
.BI \-\-desktop " NAME"
Desktop name for OnlyShowIn (default WindowMaker).
